  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'BUMPER KICK

    Line up behind the upright football and drive into it.
    The truck is the kicking foot. Actual bumper speed, angle, contact point and
    spin determine the kick. No launch button and no airborne ball control.


    FIVE
    ATTEMPTS each at progressively greater distances. One point for a forward center
    crossing BETWEEN uprights and ABOVE the crossbar before first airborne ground
    contact. Side/back/below/wide entries are not goals. A real post/crossbar ricochet
    followed by a legal forward crossing counts. Swept crossing prevents fast tunneling;
    physics contact chronology takes precedence over callback order. Once GOOD, later
    collisions cannot revoke it. Tied leaders receive equal-opportunity extra rounds
    cycling the same five distances; first shooter rotates. All participants use
    the same goal geometry, wind and contact rules.


    SOLO PRACTICE selects a
    fixed distance and keeps retrying. Practice keeps the established bumper-kick
    personal best. Sequential hot seat may reuse a keyboard or controller; inactive
    players cannot affect the attempt. AI drives into the same real contacts without
    homing or direct score awards. Actual-motion replay has angle, slow/normal/fast,
    rewind and skip. Pause/reconnect preserves the attempt; release inputs before
    fresh confirmation.


    WEATHER: choose Random or any installed forecast before
    starting. One forecast lasts the match; only Random rerolls on rematch. Actual
    wind and gusts affect drag and spin throughout flight, and wet/snow conditions
    reduce truck grip. The MPH card and windsock show the same wind; its arrow is
    relative to the camera view. Offline only.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
